                <pb facs="0501" n="413" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg413"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">721.23/805: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-01-21T10:00:00-05:00">January 21, 1933—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 3:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>21. My 19, January 17, 5 p.m. Colombian Government has delayed sending note to
                    Kellogg Pact signatories in order to give every opportunity for Brazilian
                    negotiations and avoid injuring sensibilities of Brazilian Minister for Foreign
                    Affairs. Although Mello Franco admits completely unsatisfactory nature of
                    Peruvian reply he still requests that Colombia take no steps to interrupt his
                    mediation. Notwithstanding this Colombia intends to transmit Kellogg note
                    today.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
